# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Line endings.
#
# This repository is edited on Windows (Git Bash / MobaXterm) and executed on a
# Linux HPC cluster (davinci-1, PBS). Git's default on Windows is
# core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout. For .py that is
# merely untidy -- Python 3 accepts universal newlines -- but for any file read
# BY its shebang (.sh/.pbs/.slurm) it is FATAL: bash reads the trailing CR as
# part of the interpreter name and fails with
#
#     /bin/bash^M: bad interpreter: No such file or directory
#
# Declaring eol=lf here OVERRIDES core.autocrlf for every clone on every
# machine, so nobody has to remember to configure it. Mirrors the rule already
# present in Deep-Summary-Network.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* text=auto eol=lf

*.py     text eol=lf
*.sh     text eol=lf
*.pbs    text eol=lf
*.slurm  text eol=lf
*.json   text eol=lf
*.md     text eol=lf
*.txt    text eol=lf
*.yml    text eol=lf
*.yaml   text eol=lf

# Never let Git touch these.
*.png     binary
*.pdf     binary
*.pt      binary
*.pth     binary
*.npz     binary
*.npy     binary
*.parquet binary
